    {
      "id": "c472a637-7d32-455b-b8f9-df6641b24956",
      "name": "Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "### How it works\nTwo lanes. (1) Invoice intake: a webhook receives an uploaded invoice file; the workflow validates the file type, extracts the text (PDF OCR), and an AI information extractor pulls the vendor, date, line items and totals. It then checks Google Sheets for duplicates and validates the totals \u2014 clean invoices post straight to your accounting software via HTTP (the QuickBooks/Xero endpoint you configure), while anything suspicious lands in a human review queue with an email alert to the owner. (2) Review queue reminder: every morning at 8 AM it emails the owner a list of invoices still sitting in \"review\" status so nothing gets forgotten.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your own credentials (every credential slot is a placeholder \u2014 nothing is included): OpenAI, Google Sheets, Gmail.\n2. Fill both CONFIG nodes: owner email, log sheet ID.\n3. Create a Google Sheets tab named Invoices.\n4. Edit the \"Post to Accounting - HTTP\" node with your QuickBooks/Xero endpoint + auth.\n5. Activate the workflow and point your upload form or email parser at the Invoice Webhook production URL."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
